- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/spheresample.html
- Summary (EN): Sphere Sample maps a latitude-longitude layer onto a sphere by looking up each output pixel's colour from a spherical direction or a sphere intersection. It acts like an environment backdrop or wraps an image around a transformable ball.
- Résumé (FR) : Sphere Sample projette une carte latitude-longitude sur une sphère, soit en fond d'environnement, soit en image enroulée sur une sphère transformable.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref (optional): reference layer setting output resolution and the camera and view metadata used for sampling", "source: layer sampled as the latitude-longitude sphere map"]

- Key parameters: ["Celestial Sphere: on samples the source as a sphere at infinity (environment map), off samples a transformable unit sphere and outputs a hit mask", "Filter: sampling method from Point (nearest) to Bilinear, Mitchell, B-spline and others", "Projection: Perspective (rays from camera) or Orthographic (parallel rays), used only when Celestial Sphere is off", "Translate, Rotate, Scale, Uniform Scale: transform of the sampled sphere", "Transform Order: order in which transform components are applied", "Outputs: transform (source sampled onto the sphere) and mask (1 where the sphere is hit)"]

- Caveats: ["With Celestial Sphere on, only Rotate affects the sampled direction, Translate and Scale have no effect", "In Celestial Sphere mode the mask output is 1 everywhere", "Introduced in Houdini 22.0"]

